usage: senfd [-h] [--output OUTPUT] [--dump-schema]
             [--skip-figures SKIP_FIGURES] [--version]
             [document ...]

Reads specification documents, .pdf or .docx, extracts and
normalises their figures, and makes a structured data model of
them; senfd-query lint lists what reading them found.

positional arguments:
  document              path to one or more document(s)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT       directory where the output will be saved
  --dump-schema         dump schema(s) and exit
  --skip-figures SKIP_FIGURES
                        TOML file of figures to leave out, see below
  --version             print the version and exit

--skip-figures names a TOML file of figures to leave out, each by a regular
expression of its caption and the number of figures it must match:

  [[skip]]
  regex = "^Byte, Word, and Dword Relationships$"
  matches = 1
  description = "why it is left out"

skiplists/ in senfd's repository holds those of the ratified documents.
